[I]CSV Update Metadata[/I] is a small plugin to facilitate the mass updating of the books metadata in your Calibre library.
This plugin also allow to export data of selected books into a CSV.

After load a CSV, select which column from the file to search in a library field to match the books to be updated, and associate which columns to use to update the fields, with different search and update options.

The plugin has the following features:
[LIST]
[*]Export data of selected books
[*]Preview source CSV content
[*]Preview library update
[*]Strong data validation before update

[*]Match options:[LIST]
[*]Case insensitive
[*]Case sensitive
[*]Calibre search
[/LIST]

[*]Update options:[LIST]
[*]Series-type fields include index
[*]Append value for tags-type fields
[*]Do not change the case if existing
[/LIST]

[*]Tolerate a wide range of differents CSV specifications
[/LIST]

This plugin attempt to be a autnomous version and replacement of the similar feature in [URL=https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=269911]Job Spy[/URL] by DaltonST. The only main unported feature is the support of SQL snippet and regex, however this plugin support the use of the Calibre search.

[B]Special Notes:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][COLOR="Red"][B]You can destroy your library using this plugin.[/B] Changes are permanent. There is no undo function. You are strongly encouraged to back up your library before proceeding.[/COLOR]
[/LIST]

[B]Installation[/B]
Open [I]Preferences -> Plugins -> Get new plugins[/I] and install the "Comments Cleaner" plugin.
You may also download the attached zip file and install the plugin manually, then restart calibre as described in the [URL="https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=118680"]Introduction to plugins thread[/URL]

The plugin works for Calibre 5 and later.

Page: [URL=https://github.com/un-pogaz/CSV-Update-Metadata]GitHub[/URL] | [URL=https://www.mobileread.com/forums/showthread.php?t=375984]MobileRead[/URL]

